      "after_first_return": "C05234 MOV ESI,EAX sets ESI=A1. C05236 TEST ESI,ESI tests that same 32-bit value. C05238 JNZ takes its edge to C05242 exactly when A1 is nonzero, assuming the sequence executes normally.",
      "test_flags": "TEST clears CF and OF, sets SF from bit31, ZF from zero, and PF from even parity of the low byte of A1; AF is undefined. MOV and the conditional branch do not alter these arithmetic flags.",
      "nonzero_edge": "With A1 nonzero, C05242 copies the still-local ESI=A1 into EAX. POP ESI at C05244 reads current SS:[Q1] and advances ESP to Q1+4; RET then reads next EIP from current SS:[Q1+4] and advances ESP to Q1+8. EAX remains A1, and these MOV/POP/RET instructions preserve the TEST arithmetic flags. The popped ESI and return target are not authenticated entry values.",
      "zero_edge_before_second_call": "With A1 zero, PUSH imm8 0x10 at C0523A sign-extends 0x10 to the 32-bit value 16, writes it at SS:[Q1-4], and leaves ESP=Q1-4. The E8 at C0523C writes return address C05241 at SS:[Q1-8] and transfers to BFBA09. The push does not authenticate an argument type/count, service, or calling convention.",
